624 0 obj
<<
/Title (Call center verification is a required step in this system. Consequently, the Verification System notifies the Call Center Agent to conduct a manual verification once the selfie check is over. After reviewing the customer's data, the call center agent verifies that the verification process was successful. The customer is then informed by the Verification System that the verification process is complete and that all verification processes have been successfully performed.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 621 0 R
/Prev 627 0 R
>>
endobj
625 0 obj
<<
/Title (Sequence  Diagram)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 621 0 R
/Next 622 0 R
>>
endobj
626 0 obj
<<
/Title (In this case, a customer uses the Remote Customer Onboarding System to successfully finish the verification procedure. When the customer starts the onboarding process, the system commences identity verification, which starts the verification process.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 621 0 R
/Prev 623 0 R
/Next 628 0 R
>>
endobj
627 0 obj
<<
/Title (The system uses the Biometric Verification Service to take a selfie after the ID is verified. The Biometric Verification Service receives the customer's selfie, examines it, and verifies that the liveness check was successful.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 621 0 R
/Prev 629 0 R
/Next 624 0 R
>>
endobj
628 0 obj
<<
/Title (To confirm the customer's identity, the Verification System first transmits their identity details to the external Mernis System. After verifying the validity of the identity data, the Mernis System sends the outcome back to the Verification System.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 621 0 R
/Prev 626 0 R
/Next 630 0 R
>>
endobj
629 0 obj
<<
/Title (The NFC/ID Verification Center is then used by the system to verify identities. The system further completes NFC verification via the NFC/ID Verification Center as an optional step because the customer's device supports NFC. The NFC verification has been successfully finished.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 621 0 R
/Prev 630 0 R
/Next 627 0 R
>>
endobj
630 0 obj
<<
/Title (The system then uses the SMS Service Provider to send a one-time password \(OTP\) to the customer's phone number. After receiving the SMS code, the client inputs it into the system. The SMS Service Provider receives the code from the Verification System and verifies its validity.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 621 0 R
/Prev 628 0 R
/Next 629 0 R
>>
endobj
